<title>CANADA: Thiessen more bullish than IMF on Canada - report.</title>
<headline>Thiessen more bullish than IMF on Canada - report.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's economy might better the International Monetary Fund's bullish prediction of 3.2 percent growth in 1997 in the Canadian economy, Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen was quoted as saying on Saturday.</p>
<p>The Canadian Press news agency quoted him as saying in Washington: &quot;It might be even better.&quot; The Canadian dollar could also strengthen, it reported the central bank governor as saying.</p>
</text>
